					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thelordsavant" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2992514); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2992514&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606984872" alt="TheLordSavant" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2992514)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thelordsavant" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2992514); return false;" >TheLordSavant</a></span> <span class="odate time_1496337565 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 Jun 2017 17:19</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2838872">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Reasons</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>First and main reason was because of plot convenience. It would have been less entertaining (and shorter) had they realized the truth immediately.</li>
<li>Second reason is because of unnecessary risk. The Foundation has 22 personnel afflicted. Due to the decent supply of test subjects, why waste a D-class that could be better used elsewhere? And these people are trained, possibly even highly trained. Why put their lives into the equation without taking other, less risky routes first? The researcher got tired of the blocks and of the pussy-footing of the Foundation; he pointed out this possiblity of no risk and volunteered to put his life at risk.</li>
<li>Third reason is because previous experience. The entity who wrote this is known for making these anomalous novels and releasing them to the mainstream. This indicates that it has semi-malicious intent in mind. Though the primary hazard is on the cover, the very releasing of the book appears actively harmful. It is reasonable to assume that there would be more to it than simply the cover.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>But basically, it boils down to plot convinience. If you have ideas for writing the article to be more logically sound, feel free to suggest them. I'd be happy to make the change if it improves the article.</p>

							</div>

								
					
